@@ -33,4 +33,9 @@ The saved-address update requests browser geolocation automatically when there i
 
 Registration now captures name as well as phone, area and full delivery address. A successful server discovery saves its normalized context with the customer name under `fasakhansta.web.customer.v1`. On the same device/browser, the upper address selector restores the selected name, phone, address and coordinates without another GPS request. It offers a new address and a clear-local-details action. Restored records are type/length/bounds validated, safely rendered, deduplicated and bounded to ten. They never bypass discovery, coverage or price validation, and cannot be retrieved by a public phone lookup. Browser storage refusal displays a useful notice while allowing ordering. Clearing site data or using another browser requires registration again.
 
-Use the dedicated `deployment/install_web_customer_addresses.py` patch for this update: only the homepage and two storefront assets are changed, with three-way homepage merging to retain independent SEO changes, source hashes, backup and rollback. It runs only `artisan view:clear`, without a database migration or route changes. Success: `WEB_CUSTOMER_ADDRESSES_READY`. The DOM suite also verifies automatic/denied/late GPS, profile recall, address history, malformed/blocked storage, safe rendering, checkout name prefill and pending-order recovery.
+Use the dedicated `deployment/install_web_customer_addresses.py` patch for this update: the homepage and two storefront assets are changed by the first customer release, with three-way homepage merging to retain independent SEO changes, source hashes, backup and rollback. It runs only `artisan view:clear`, without a database migration or route changes. Success: `WEB_CUSTOMER_ADDRESSES_READY`. The DOM suite also verifies automatic/denied/late GPS, profile recall, address history, malformed/blocked storage, safe rendering, checkout name prefill and pending-order recovery.
+
+
+Returning visitors now activate the last saved address with an automatic server discovery request; they do not resubmit or reconfirm registration. The address selector lives in the persistent site header. Selecting another saved address with an empty cart immediately rediscovers eligible stores. A nonempty cart keeps the existing clear-cart confirmation, and adding/editing an address still opens the data form. Failed automatic discovery keeps the saved summary and offers retry without asking for registration again. An uncertain prior order must be resolved before automatic discovery starts. This incremental patch requires the previous customer/address release `2c597530e88c78e39f54bc68351246732a566fa2`; it preserves its browser storage schema and saved data.
+
+The automatic-return patch additionally preserves the server session context nonce when normalized delivery fields are unchanged. Reopening the same address in another tab therefore does not invalidate an in-flight quote. Different or invalid delivery details still invalidate the former context, and every automatic discovery still rechecks current coverage. The incremental installer scopes its four files to home, storefront JS/CSS, and the existing WebStorefront service; it syntax-checks both PHP targets and performs no migration.
